Subject: [PATCH 1201/1252] HERESY 1169: the Writer's OpenRouter models with
 their prices, as you type
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The rc3 list: «The Writer's models with their prices, from OpenRouter's list, as you type». The page fetched OpenRouter's
list (467 models today, CORS open) for the field's suggestions, ids alone. Each model now carries its price per million
tokens in and out and its context: in the suggestions as you type (Chrome shows an option's label beside it), in a line
under the field for the one chosen (amber, «not in OpenRouter's list», for a name it does not know), and in the quick
picks' tips. A price of 0 is «free», a negative one (a router's) «the price varies». The guide in seven languages says so.

Kitchen suite: 396 passed, 0 failed, 7 skipped (a check feeds a list of its own, so it does not hang on the internet).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
